  "diagnostics": "Early feature helpers collided with inherited PHPUnit/Laravel methods, then were renamed. An initial HTTP fake appended to the original wildcard500 and hid positive GET fixtures; fixtures now reset the Factory before lookup, without changing assertions. Focused37 and initial native39 runs preceded final added UI/cap/timeout coverage and are diagnostics, not the final source matrix. Acceptance launch commands initially named nonexistent native/static paths and ran no such test cases; final profiles use the actual prior accepted selection plus the new lookup classes. The first complete four-database mixed-class run then exposed a real harness isolation error: a committed GLO fixture from a preceding truncation class made a later RefreshDatabase empty-result assumption false. That failing matrix is retained as diagnostics. The final full runner gives every source test file its own process and disposable SQLite database, with eight workers and four disjoint aggregate reports. No application/test assertion was changed or filtered for this correction. Final acceptance covers every discovered ID on the unchanged frozen implementation. Isolated controls intentionally fail assertions; these are not application regression failures.",
  "scope": "Local synthetic application acceptance; default/native profiles overlap and skips remain explicit. The new two-child witness is at the wallet lock before the initial original snapshot: it proves real SQL contention and one resulting receipt, not a forced both-GETs-before-custody or creator-response-versus-lookup interleave. Late projection faults are injected exceptions, not process-kill/power-loss certification. Receipt verification is required for a nonnull attempt marker; a marker-null orphan receipt from trusted arbitrary DB tampering is not separately detected. No universal concurrent permission-writer closure, arbitrary SQL/key administrator protection, live provider call, customer funds movement, production migration, remote CI execution, merchant approval, refunds/disputes or worldwide certification. Positive session discovery is not settlement or provider-confirmed negative/failure release. Those remaining protocols are listed explicitly in docs/remaining-work-part-54.md."
